WEBVTT

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:03.080
SIEM platforms are powerful, but they are not magic.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:07.000
Poorly configured SIEM environments may generate excessive false positives or fail to

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.705
detect important activity.

00:00:08.705 --> 00:00:13.270
Collecting too much data without prioritization can overwhelm analysts and increase noise.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.485
Missing data sources create blind spots.

00:00:15.485 --> 00:00:18.425
Correlation rules require maintenance and refinement as environments change.

00:00:18.425 --> 00:00:22.080
A useful alert today may become noisy after an application update,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.480
while a new cloud service may need new log sources and detection logic.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.550
Organizations also need trained personnel who understand how to investigate alerts and

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:30.998
improve detections over time.

00:00:30.998 --> 00:00:35.555
SIEM technology supports security operations, but people and processes remain essential.

00:00:35.555 --> 00:00:38.485
The value comes from thoughtful configuration, ongoing tuning,

00:00:38.485 --> 00:00:39.920
and disciplined investigation.
